1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,476
Quick question.

2
00:00:01,516 --> 00:00:02,569
Why do we
never say

3
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:04,215
furnitures,
equipments,

4
00:00:04,255 --> 00:00:05,568
or luggages?

5
00:00:06,703 --> 00:00:09,093
Watch. Here’s
an empty room.

6
00:00:10,037 --> 00:00:11,971
In comes a chair.

7
00:00:13,903 --> 00:00:15,405
Then a sofa.

8
00:00:17,337 --> 00:00:18,743
Then a bed.

9
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,385
Now the room
has furniture.

10
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:23,875
Not three
furnitures.

11
00:00:23,915 --> 00:00:25,332
Just furniture.

12
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:28,150
English doesn’t
name each piece.

13
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:30,252
It groups them
into one unit.

14
00:00:30,292 --> 00:00:31,934
And a unit
means one.

15
00:00:31,974 --> 00:00:33,378
One is always
singular,

16
00:00:33,418 --> 00:00:36,140
so no s:
the furniture is new.

17
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:39,007
Now a mechanic’s
workshop,

18
00:00:39,047 --> 00:00:40,804
and an empty
toolbox.

19
00:00:41,537 --> 00:00:43,327
A spanner goes in.

20
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:46,772
Then a hammer.

21
00:00:48,703 --> 00:00:50,253
Then a drill.

22
00:00:52,003 --> 00:00:53,128
Close the lid.

23
00:00:53,168 --> 00:00:54,649
Many tools,
one box,

24
00:00:54,689 --> 00:00:56,834
one unit:
equipment.

25
00:00:56,874 --> 00:00:58,473
So: the equipment
is ready.

26
00:00:59,403 --> 00:01:00,933
Now someone
is getting ready

27
00:01:00,973 --> 00:01:02,753
for the airport.

28
00:01:03,503 --> 00:01:05,413
First, a suitcase.

29
00:01:07,337 --> 00:01:09,031
Then a backpack.

30
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:12,880
Then
a carry-on bag.

31
00:01:14,603 --> 00:01:16,258
Bags and suitcases
together

32
00:01:16,298 --> 00:01:17,475
make one unit:

33
00:01:17,515 --> 00:01:18,898
luggage. So:

34
00:01:18,938 --> 00:01:20,521
my luggage
is heavy.

35
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:22,404
Need a number?

36
00:01:22,444 --> 00:01:23,630
Count a piece:

37
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:25,204
two pieces
of furniture,

38
00:01:25,244 --> 00:01:26,389
a piece
of equipment,

39
00:01:26,429 --> 00:01:28,180
three pieces
of luggage.

40
00:01:28,903 --> 00:01:30,809
So don’t memorise
the list.

41
00:01:30,849 --> 00:01:31,959
See the unit:

42
00:01:31,999 --> 00:01:33,362
many things,
one name,

43
00:01:33,402 --> 00:01:34,701
one verb.

